const e=JSON.parse(`[{"id":"LR_E1A_Q001","exercise":"exercise_1a","type":"linear_arrangement","is_set":false,"question_text":"Five people L, M, N, O and P sit in a row, not necessarily in the same order. P sits exactly in between M and N. If L sits exactly in between M and O, then which of the following must be true?","options":{"A":"O sits to the immediate right of M.","B":"L and N always sit together.","C":"M sits exactly at the center of the row.","D":"P sits between M and L."},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"M sits exactly at the center of the row.","solution_text":"Five people L, M, N, O, and P sit in a row, not necessarily in the same order. P sits exactly between M and N which means that the following arrangements can be obtained: M/N P M/N L/O L/O (or) L/O M/N P M/N L/O (or) L/O L/O M/N P M/N It is also given that L sits exactly between M and O, which means that M sits at the center of the row. N P M L O (or) O L M P N \\"M sits exactly at the center of the row\\" is true.","entity_count":5,"variables":1,"constraints":2,"case_splits":3,"resolution_type":"multiple","resolution_count":2,"information_load":"low","solving_methodologies":["case_elimination"],"question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E1A_Q002","exercise":"exercise_1a","type":"linear_arrangement","is_set":false,"question_text":"Six persons Tanmay, Sanjay, Ganpat, Dhruv, Nagraj and Jivan are standing in a queue at a railway ticket counter. Further it is known that (i) Ganpat is two positions ahead Jivan. (ii) only Nagraj is ahead Tanmay. (iii) neither Sanjay nor Jivan is standing at the end of the queue. How many persons are ahead of Dhruv but behind Tanmay?","options":{"A":"Zero","B":"Two","C":"Three","D":"Four"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Three","solution_text":"From (ii), we can say that Nagraj is the first person in the queue while Tanmay is the second. Now, from (i) and (iii) we can say that Ganpat is the 3rd person and Jivan is 5th. Thus, Sanjay is the 4th person and Dhruv is the last person in the queue. Hence the queue is Nagraj Tanmay Ganpat Sanjay Jivan Dhruv There are 3 persons (Ganpat, Sanjay and Jivan) ahead of Dhruv but behind Tanmay.","entity_count":6,"variables":1,"constraints":3,"case_splits":1,"resolution_type":"single","information_load":"low","solving_methodologies":["linear_sequencing"],"question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"easy","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E1A_Q003","exercise":"exercise_1a","type":"linear_arrangement","is_set":false,"question_text":"The Principal called five persons Srinivas, Murali, Raghu, Vijay and Krishna who are Director, Secretary, Treasurer, Professor and Student Leader of a college, not necessarily in that order. They are seated in the five seats facing the Principal. The Treasurer sat to the immediate left of Krishna who is one seat away from the Director. Murali is two places away from the Secretary. Vijay, who is the Student Leader, is one place to the right of Murali. What is the position of Krishna with respect to the Professor?","options":{"A":"To the immediate right.","B":"Three places away to the left.","C":"Two places away to the left.","D":"Cannot be determined"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Cannot be determined","solution_text":"It is given that: _________ Krishna ________ Treasurer Director As Murali is two places away from the Secretary and Vijay sits to the immediate right of Murali, we have two cases _______ Krishna ______ Murali Vijay Treasurer Secretary Director Proff. Student Leader (or) _______ Krishna Murali Vijay _____ Treasurer Proff. Director Student Leader Secretary Position of Krishna with respect to the Professor is different in different cases as shown above. So, it cannot be determined.","entity_count":5,"variables":2,"constraints":4,"case_splits":2,"resolution_type":"multiple","resolution_count":2,"information_load":"medium","solving_methodologies":["multi_constraint_balancing"],"question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E1A_Q004","exercise":"exercise_1a","type":"linear_arrangement","is_set":false,"question_text":"Seven men, A, B, C, D, E, F and G have parked their cars in a row. The cars of E and F should be next to each other. The cars of D and G should be parked next to each other. Whereas A and B cannot park their cars next to each other. But B and D must park their cars next to each other and C's car is parked to the immediate right of G's car. If E parks his car to the left of F, then which of the following statements is false?","options":{"A":"There are two cars in between B and G's cars.","B":"B and C's cars are not parked together.","C":"G's car is the only car in between D and C's cars.","D":"A's car is at the left extreme end."},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"There are two cars in between B and G's cars.","solution_text":"A, B, C, D, E, F and G are seven persons who parked their cars in a row. E's car and F's car should be next to each other, i.e. EF or FE. Similarly the cars of D and G should be next to each other, i.e. DG or GD. A's car and B's car should not be next to each other, whereas the cars of B and D are parked next to each other, i.e. BD or DB. C's car is parked to the immediate right of G's, i.e. G → C. Hence, they can be parked in the following order. (i) E F or F E (ii) D G or G D (iii) B D G (iv) B D G C As A and B are not parked together, the arrangement can be as follows, (i) A - - B D G C (ii) - A - B D G C (iii) - - B D G C A (iv) - B D G C A - (v) - B D G C - A (vi) B D G C A - - (vii) B D G C - A - (viii) B D G C - - A But as E and F must be together, the arrangement can be as follows. AFEBDGC or AEFBDGC FEBDGCA (or) EFBDGCA BDGCA (EF or FE) or BDGC (EF or FE) A If E and F park in that order only, i.e. E first and then F, then the order is EFBDGCA (or) BDGCAEF. In any case B and D have only one car between their cars. Choice (A) is FALSE. B and C do not park together. Choice (B) is TRUE. D and C have only G's car between their cars. Choice (C) is TRUE. A is at the extreme. Choice (D) is partly true.","entity_count":7,"variables":1,"constraints":5,"case_splits":4,"resolution_type":"multiple","resolution_count":2,"information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["case_elimination","linear_sequencing"],"question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"set_id":"LR_E1A_S5_7","exercise":"exercise_1a","type":"linear_arrangement","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. Five persons – Amit, Balram, Chetan, Deepak and Eswar are sitting in a row facing North. The following information is known about them. (i) Only Deepak is sitting between Amit and Balram. (ii) Neither Amit nor Balram is at the ends. (iii) Chetan is sitting to the immediate left of Balram.","setup_solution":"From (i) and (ii), we have __ A/B D B/A ___ From (iii) we can say that C must be at the left end of the row. Thus, we get the following arrangement. C B D A E","entity_count":5,"variables":1,"constraints":3,"case_splits":1,"resolution_type":"single","information_load":"low","solving_methodologies":["linear_sequencing"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E1A_Q005","question_text":"Who is sitting at the right end of the row?","options":{"A":"Amit","B":"Balaram","C":"Chetan","D":"Eswar"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Eswar","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"easy","time_benchmark_seconds":45},{"id":"LR_E1A_Q006","question_text":"How many persons are sitting between Amit and Chetan?","options":{"A":"Zero","B":"One","C":"Two","D":"Three"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Two","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"easy","time_benchmark_seconds":45},{"id":"LR_E1A_Q007","question_text":"What is the position of Eswar with respect to Balram?","options":{"A":"Immediate right.","B":"Second to the left.","C":"Third to the right.","D":"Immediate left."},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Third to the right.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"easy","time_benchmark_seconds":45}]},{"set_id":"LR_E1A_S8_10","exercise":"exercise_1a","type":"linear_arrangement","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. Six persons P, Q, R, S, T and U are sitting in a row facing North. Further it is known that: (i) Exactly two persons are sitting between P and Q. (ii) Exactly one person is sitting between T and U. (iii) Q is sitting at the right end of the row.","setup_solution":"From (i) and (iii), we get __ __ P __ __ Q Now, from (ii) and the above, we can say that the person sitting between T and U is P. Hence we get 4 possible arrangements which are as follows. R T P U S Q ----- Case (a) R U P T S Q ----- Case (b) S T P U R Q ----- Case (c) S U P T R Q ----- Case (d)","entity_count":6,"variables":1,"constraints":3,"case_splits":4,"resolution_type":"multiple","resolution_count":4,"information_load":"medium","solving_methodologies":["case_elimination"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E1A_Q008","question_text":"If U is sitting adjacent to S, then how many persons are sitting between U and R?","options":{"A":"One","B":"Two","C":"Three","D":"Cannot be determined"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Two","solution_text":"U is adjacent to S in cases (a) and (d), and in both the cases there are two persons sitting between U and R.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":75},{"id":"LR_E1A_Q009","question_text":"If S is sitting to the immediate right of T, then who is sitting second to the right of R?","options":{"A":"P","B":"T","C":"U","D":"S"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"P","solution_text":"S is sitting to the immediate right of T in case (b), Hence, P is sitting second to the right of R.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":75},{"id":"LR_E1A_Q010","question_text":"Who among the following cannot be adjacent to T?","options":{"A":"P","B":"R","C":"S","D":"None of these"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"None of these","solution_text":"All the three P, R and S, can be adjacent to T.","question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":60}]},{"set_id":"LR_E1A_S11_13","exercise":"exercise_1a","type":"linear_arrangement","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. Eight books on different subjects- Biology, Chemistry, Physics, Maths, English, Hindi, Zoology and Economics are stacked together. Further it is known that (i) Economics is above Biology, which is just above Hindi, which is not at the bottom. (ii) There are only two books between the Zoology and the English books. (iii) Number of books above Chemistry is less than the number of books below it. (iv) Only Maths book is above Zoology.","setup_solution":"From (ii) and (iv) we can say that Maths is on the top, Zoology is 2nd from the top, and English is 5th from the top. Now from (i) we can say that Hindi is 2nd from the bottom and Biology is 3rd from the bottom. Now, from above information and (iii), Economics and Chemistry are the 3rd and 4th from the top. Thus, Physics is the bottom one in the stack. Hence we have the following arrangement. Maths Zoology Economics/Chemistry Chemistry/Economics English Biology Hindi Physics","entity_count":8,"variables":1,"constraints":4,"case_splits":1,"resolution_type":"single","information_load":"medium","solving_methodologies":["linear_sequencing"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E1A_Q011","question_text":"Which book is at the bottom of the stack?","options":{"A":"Physics","B":"Hindi","C":"English","D":"Economics"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Physics","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"easy","time_benchmark_seconds":60},{"id":"LR_E1A_Q012","question_text":"How many books are there between Economics and Hindi?","options":{"A":"Three","B":"Two","C":"Four","D":"Cannot be determined"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Cannot be determined","solution_text":"Position of Economics book is not certain, and hence cannot be determined.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":60},{"id":"LR_E1A_Q013","question_text":"Find the pair that does not exhibit a similar relationship as the other three pairs.","options":{"A":"Biology – Hindi","B":"Economics – Chemistry","C":"English – Hindi","D":"Maths – Zoology"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"English – Hindi","solution_text":"Except English – Hindi all other pairs are in adjacent positions.","question_operation":"odd_one_out","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":75}]},{"set_id":"LR_E1A_S14_16","exercise":"exercise_1a","type":"linear_arrangement","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. Four persons A, B, C and D are sitting in row I facing South and four other persons P, Q, R and S are sitting in row II facing North. Each person in row I is facing exactly one person in row II. The following information is also known about them. (i) P is sitting opposite C and D is not sitting opposite S. (ii) A is sitting diagonally opposite R. (iii) B is second to the right of C.","setup_solution":"From (ii) and (iii) we get two possible cases Case (a) A B C R Case (b) B C A R Case (a) is not possible as C is sitting opposite P (from (i)). Hence, case (b) is possible. Now from (i) we get the position of P. From (iv) we can say that S is opposite A and hence Q is opposite D. Thus, we get the following arrangement. B D C A Row I R W P S Row II","entity_count":8,"variables":2,"constraints":3,"case_splits":2,"resolution_type":"single","information_load":"medium","solving_methodologies":["case_elimination","multi_constraint_balancing"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E1A_Q014","question_text":"Who is sitting opposite S?","options":{"A":"A","B":"B","C":"C","D":"D"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"A","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":60},{"id":"LR_E1A_Q015","question_text":"Which of the following is the correct order of persons sitting in Row I from right to left?","options":{"A":"ACDB","B":"ADCB","C":"BDCA","D":"BCDA"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"BDCA","solution_text":"Persons in Row I from right to left BDCA.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":60},{"id":"LR_E1A_Q016","question_text":"Who among the following is adjacent to Q but not opposite B?","options":{"A":"P","B":"R","C":"S","D":"Cannot be determined"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"P","solution_text":"P and R are adjacent to Q. But R is opposite B. Hence, the correct answer is P.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":75}]},{"set_id":"LR_E1A_S17_19","exercise":"exercise_1a","type":"linear_arrangement","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. There are nine members – Anup, Bagha, Dulal, Elena, Fuli, Gopal, Harsh, Indira and Ketan, in a Kho-Kho team. All are sitting in a row, such that any two adjacent people are facing opposite directions. Elena is adjacent to Indira and Anup. Ketan is adjacent to Fuli and Gopal. Bagha and Dulal are facing the same direction, where Bagha is sitting to the left of Dulal. Harsh is sitting to the immediate right of Anup.","setup_solution":"Let us denote the persons with the first letter of their names. It is given that E is adjacent to I and A. IEA or AEI are possible → (1) Also, it is given that K is adjacent to F and G. FKG or GKF are possible → (2) From the given statement, H is to the immediate right of A and from (A) we have IEAH or HAEI → (3) Given that, B and D face the same direction. We have to adjust B and D in the row, such that (2) and (3) are not violated. Finally, from the given statement, B is to left of D, we can have the following possibilities if B and D face north. (i) B __ __ __ D __ __ __ __ (ii) B __ __ __ __ __ __ __ D (iii) __ __ __ __ B __ __ __ D As any two adjacent people face opposite directions, we cannot place IEAH or HAEI in possibility (i). If B and D face South, consider HAEI case: H A E I D F/G K G/F B As Harsh is sitting to the immediate right of Anup, Anup is facing south. So, I is also facing south which is a contradicting the condition “any two adjacent people are facing opposite directions” (I and D are both facing South). Consider IEAH case: I E A H D F/G K G/F B As Harsh is sitting to the immediate right of Anup, Anup is facing north. So, H is facing south which is a contradicting the condition “any two adjacent people are facing opposite directions” (H and D both are facing South). So, B and D cannot face South. (a) B F/G K G/F I E A H D (b) B F/G K G/F H A E I D (c) I E A H B F/G K G/F D (d) H A E I B F/G K G/F D","entity_count":9,"variables":2,"constraints":5,"case_splits":4,"resolution_type":"multiple","resolution_count":4,"information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["case_elimination","multi_constraint_balancing"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E1A_Q017","question_text":"Who does not sit at any of the ends?","options":{"A":"Bagha","B":"Fuli","C":"Dulal","D":"Indira"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Fuli","solution_text":"In none of the cases Fuli is at the end.","question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E1A_Q018","question_text":"If Fuli is facing south, then who among the following will face North?","options":{"A":"Dulal","B":"Harsh","C":"Elena","D":"None of these"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Dulal","solution_text":"In all the cases Fuli and Dulal face the opposite direction.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E1A_Q019","question_text":"What is the minimum number of people that can sit between Bagha and Indira?","options":{"A":"0","B":"2","C":"3","D":"More than 3"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"0","solution_text":"In case (d), Bagha and Indira are adjacent.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90}]},{"set_id":"LR_E1A_S20_22","exercise":"exercise_1a","type":"linear_arrangement","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. Nine persons A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H and I are seated in a row, not necessarily in the same order. Following is some information regarding the seating arrangement. (i) A is seated as many places to the left of C as D is seated to the right of B. (ii) The only person seated between F and H is seated two places to the left of I. (iii) Neither C nor D is seated at any of the ends. (iv) G, who is not seated at any of the ends, is seated to the right of E. (v) E and F are seated together.","setup_solution":"(a) Position 1 → C, D, G, I Position 9 → A, B, C, D, E, F, H, G (b) F – HI OR H – FI (c) Since, A, B, C, D, E, F, G, H are not seated at the extreme right ends, I must be seated there. _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ I (d) _ _ _ _ _ F _ H I or _ _ _ _ _ H _ F I Hence, position 1 → C, D, G, H, F, E, I, L so it is either A or B. Since E and F are seated together, the following possibilities can exist. (i) A C B D E F G H I (ii) A B C D E F G H I (iii) B D A C E F G H I (iv) B A D C E F G H I","entity_count":9,"variables":1,"constraints":5,"case_splits":4,"resolution_type":"multiple","resolution_count":4,"information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["multi_constraint_balancing","case_elimination"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E1A_Q020","question_text":"In how many ways can these nine persons be seated?","options":{"A":"Two","B":"Four","C":"One","D":"Three"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Four","solution_text":"There are four ways.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E1A_Q021","question_text":"Which of the following is definitely TRUE?","options":{"A":"D and E are seated together.","B":"C is seated to the left of D.","C":"F and G are seated together.","D":"A and B are seated together."},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"F and G are seated together.","solution_text":"Choice (A): D and E are not seated together in (iii) and (iv). Choice (B): C is to right of D in (iii) and (iv). Choice (C): F and G are seated together in all the cases from (i) to (iv). Choice (D): A and B are not seated together in case (i) and (iii).","question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E1A_Q022","question_text":"Which one of the following may be a valid representation of the seating positions of the person? (a) B A D C E F G H I (b) B D A C E F G H I (c) A B C D E F G H I (d) A C B D E F G H I","options":{"A":"(a), (b), (c) and (d)","B":"(a) and (d) only","C":"(b) and (c) only","D":"(a), (b) and (d) only"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"(a), (b), (c) and (d)","solution_text":"By observing the cases (i) through (iv), all the four are valid representations.","question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90}]},{"set_id":"LR_E1A_S23_26","exercise":"exercise_1a","type":"linear_arrangement","is_set":true,"setup_text":"There are eight people A to H each one seated in one among the nine chairs, facing north. It is further known that: I. None among E, C and D is either at the ends or adjacent to one another. II. There are three chairs to the left of A and three persons to the right of B. Neither of A and B is adjacent to the vacant seat. III. F is at the left end of the row while G is to the immediate left of H.","setup_solution":"II and III can be written as: F __ __ A __ B __ __ __ Or F __ __ A B __ __ __ __ As E and C and D are not in the corners, H is in the corner and G is to the immediate left of H. As the vacant chair cannot be adjacent to either A or B, E, C and D cannot be accommodated in the non-adjacent seats using second case. Therefore, the final arrangement would be: F Vac E/C/D A E/C/D B E/C/D G H","entity_count":8,"variables":2,"constraints":3,"case_splits":2,"resolution_type":"multiple","resolution_count":6,"information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["multi_constraint_balancing","case_elimination"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E1A_Q023","question_text":"In how many ways, can these eight people be seated?","options":{"A":"Two","B":"Six","C":"Four","D":"One"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Six","solution_text":"There are total 3! = 6 possible arrangements.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E1A_Q024","question_text":"Who among the following is sitting at the end?","options":{"A":"H","B":"C","C":"G","D":"A"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"H","solution_text":"H is sitting in the corner seat.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":60},{"id":"LR_E1A_Q025","question_text":"If both E and D are adjacent to A, then, who among the following is adjacent to B?","options":{"A":"F","B":"G","C":"C","D":"A"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"C","solution_text":"C is adjacent to B as E, and D would be adjacent to A.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E1A_Q026","question_text":"What is the position of the vacant chair with respect to A?","options":{"A":"Immediate left","B":"Immediate right","C":"Second to the left","D":"Second to the right"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Second to the left","solution_text":"The vacant chair is second to the left with respect to A.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":60}]},{"set_id":"LR_E1A_S27_30","exercise":"exercise_1a","type":"linear_arrangement","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. There are three doctors, three engineers and two teachers among eight friends A to H who are sitting in a row. Some of them are facing north while the other are facing south. It is also known that: I. All the people of same profession are neither sitting together nor facing the same direction. II. There are at least four people between A and F. A and F belong to the same profession. III. Neither D nor E is an engineer. IV. There is a doctor to the Immediate right of every teacher while there is a teacher to the immediate left of every doctor. V. B, the doctor is sitting in one of the ends is sitting second to the left an other doctor who is facing north. VI. Neither a teacher nor a doctor is to the left of one of the engineers. VII. C is to the immediate right of D while C, E and H are facing the same direction.","setup_solution":"Note the following representation: Doctor – Dr, Teacher – Tr and Engineer – Er From IV and V we get: B(Dr)↓ (Tr) Dr↑ __ __ __ __ __ (1) (2) (3) (4) (5) (6) (7) (8) From (VI), one of the engineers is in position (8) and is facing south. From (II), if one of A and F is in potion (2), the other should be in position (7) or (8). But, A and F cannot be in (2) and (8) as both are of the same profession. A and F cannot be in (3) and (8) for the same reason that they both belong to the same profession. Hence, they can be in (2) and (7), both being teachers. Now, we know that A and F are the two teachers and B is a doctor. From III, D and E are doctors and C, H and G are engineers. One of D and E is in position (3) and the other one is in position (6) (from IV). If D is in position (3), we get the following arrangement. B(Dr)↓ A/F(Tr) D(Dr)↑ C(Er) __ __ F/A (Tr) G/H(Er)↓ (1) (2) (3) (4) (5) (6) (7) (8) From IV, E (doctor) is in position (6) facing north and the teacher in position (7) will be facing south. From I, the teacher in position (2) will be facing north. From VII, C, E and H will be facing south. Since, C and H (both engineers) are facing south, the third engineer G will be facing north. Hence, H is in position (8) and G in position (5). Thus, we get the following arrangement. B(Dr)↓ A/F(Tr)↑ D(Dr)↑ C(Er)↓ G(Er)↑ E (Dr)↓ F/A (Tr)↓ H(Er)↓ (1) (2) (3) (4) (5) (6) (7) (8) If D is in position (6), we get the following. B(Dr)↓ A/F(Tr)↑ E(Dr)↑ H(Er)↑ C(Er)↑ D(Dr)↓ F/A(Tr)↓ G(Er)↓ (1) (2) (3) (4) (5) (6) (7) (8)","entity_count":8,"variables":3,"constraints":7,"case_splits":2,"resolution_type":"multiple","resolution_count":2,"information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["multi_constraint_balancing","case_elimination"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E1A_Q027","question_text":"Who among the following is a teacher?","options":{"A":"A","B":"B","C":"C","D":"D"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"A","solution_text":"A is a teacher.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":75},{"id":"LR_E1A_Q028","question_text":"The person of which of the following professions is not sitting at any of the ends?","options":{"A":"Teacher","B":"Doctor","C":"Engineer","D":"More than one of the above"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Teacher","solution_text":"Only a teacher is not at any of the ends.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":75},{"id":"LR_E1A_Q029","question_text":"Who among the following is adjacent to an engineer but not an engineer himself?","options":{"A":"B","B":"A","C":"D","D":"C"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"D","solution_text":"D is adjacent to an engineer but not an engineer himself.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":75},{"id":"LR_E1A_Q030","question_text":"Who among the following can be at one of the ends and what is his profession?","options":{"A":"F, Teacher","B":"H, Engineer","C":"F, Doctor","D":"H, Doctor"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"H, Engineer","solution_text":"H, the engineer can be at one of the ends.","question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90}]},{"set_id":"LR_E1B_S1_3","exercise":"exercise_1b","type":"linear_arrangement","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. Seven flags of different colours − Violet, Indigo, Blue, Green, Yellow, Orange and Red – are placed in a row from left to right, not necessarily in that order. The Indigo flag and the Yellow flag have four flags between them. The Orange flag is not between the Indigo flag and the Yellow flag. Neither the Violet flag nor the Red flag is next to the Blue flag.","setup_solution":"In each arrangement above, we get 4 possibilities. Hence, the total number of possible arrangements is 16. [For Q2, building on this base:] Since, none among Black, White, Red and Violet flags is at an end, and that none among Black, White and Blue flags can be adjacent to either Red or Violet flags, one among Indigo and yellow should be at an end and orange should be at the other end. Let us consider the case where Yellow, Indigo and Orange flags are in positions 1, 6 and 9 respectively. Since Black and White are to be adjacent to each other, they can be in positions (2, 3) or (3, 4) or (4, 5) or (7, 8) in any order. Let us consider them in positions 2 and 3 in any order. Then, Red and Violet have to be in positions 7 and 8 in any order and Blue and Green in positions 4 and 5 in any order. Thus, we get 8 possible arrangements. When Black and White are in positions 3 and 4, Blue and Green will be in positions 1 and 5. Thus, we get 8 more arrangements. Similarly, when Black and White are in positions 4 and 5, Blue and Green will be in positions 2 and 3, we get 8 more arrangements. When Black and White are in position 7 and 8 in any order, Blue and Green can be in positions 2 and 3 respectively, Red and Violet in positions 4 and 5 in any order. This gives 4 arrangements. Another case is, Green and Blue in positions 4 and 5 respectively, Red and Violet in positions 2 and 3 in any order. This gives another 4 arrangements. Thus, we get 32 arrangements when Let us consider the case where Yellow. When the positions of Indigo and Yellow are interchanged, i.e they are in positions 1 and 6 respectively, we get 32 more arrangements. We get 32 more arrangements when Blue, Orange and Yellow flags are in positions 1, 4 and 9 respectively. Another 32 arrangements when they are in positions 1, 9 and 4 respectively. Thus, in all 4 x 32 = 128 arrangements are possible.","entity_count":7,"variables":1,"constraints":3,"case_splits":4,"resolution_type":"multiple","resolution_count":16,"information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["combinatorial_counting","case_elimination"],"type_specific":{"partial_resolution":true,"note":"Base set resolves to 16 valid arrangements (groups/slots rather than fixed individuals), not one fixed seating. Q2 adds two more flags and recomputes the count under additional constraints."},"questions":[{"id":"LR_E1B_Q001","question_text":"What is the total number of possible arrangements?","options":{"A":"12","B":"8","C":"4","D":"None of these"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"None of these","solution_text":"In each arrangement above, we get 4 possibilities. Hence, the total number of possible arrangements is 16.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q002","question_text":"If the Black flag and the White flag are also to be placed in the row, such that they are adjacent to each other but neither of them is next to the Violet flag or the Red flag, and also none of the Black, White, Violet, Red flags is at any of the ends, then what is the total number of possible arrangements?","options":{"A":"32","B":"64","C":"96","D":"128"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"128","solution_text":"Since, none among Black, White, Red and Violet flags is at an end, and that none among Black, White and Blue flags can be adjacent to either Red or Violet flags, one among Indigo and yellow should be at an end and orange should be at the other end. Let us consider the case where Yellow, Indigo and Orange flags are in positions 1, 6 and 9 respectively. Since Black and White are to be adjacent to each other, they can be in positions (2, 3) or (3, 4) or (4, 5) or (7, 8) in any order. Let us consider them in positions 2 and 3 in any order. Then, Red and Violet have to be in positions 7 and 8 in any order and Blue and Green in positions 4 and 5 in any order. Thus, we get 8 possible arrangements. When Black and White are in positions 3 and 4, Blue and Green will be in positions 1 and 5. Thus, we get 8 more arrangements. Similarly, when Black and White are in positions 4 and 5, Blue and Green will be in positions 2 and 3, we get 8 more arrangements. When Black and White are in position 7 and 8 in any order, Blue and Green can be in positions 2 and 3 respectively, Red and Violet in positions 4 and 5 in any order. This gives 4 arrangements. Another case is, Green and Blue in positions 4 and 5 respectively, Red and Violet in positions 2 and 3 in any order. This gives another 4 arrangements. Thus, we get 32 arrangements when Let us consider the case where Yellow. When the positions of Indigo and Yellow are interchanged, i.e they are in positions 1 and 6 respectively, we get 32 more arrangements. We get 32 more arrangements when Blue, Orange and Yellow flags are in positions 1, 4 and 9 respectively. Another 32 arrangements when they are in positions 1, 9 and 4 respectively. Thus, in all 4 x 32 = 128 arrangements are possible.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":180},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q003","question_text":"Which of the following statements is true?","options":{"A":"Yellow flag is at one of the ends.","B":"The Indigo flag and the Orange flag are adjacent to each other.","C":"The Blue flag is adjacent to the Green flag.","D":"The Yellow flag or the Indigo flag is/are adjacent to both the Orange flag and the Blue flag."},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"The Blue flag is adjacent to the Green flag.","solution_text":"(A) Yellow flag may or may not be at an extreme end, as shown in various arrangements. (B) Similarly, as shown in the figures above, Indigo and Orange flags may not be together. (C) The Blue flag is always adjacent to the Green flag, as seen in every possible arrangement. (D) This statement again may or may not be true, as can be observed in the arrangements.","question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90}]},{"set_id":"LR_E1B_S4_6","exercise":"exercise_1b","type":"linear_arrangement","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. Eight persons A, B, C, D, E, F, G and H are sitting in a row facing North. Only two persons are sitting to the left of D. A is adjacent to G and F. E is at one of the ends and three persons are sitting between him and G.","setup_solution":"Given that only two persons are sitting to the left of D, we know that D is the 3rd person from the left. Now E is at one of the ends. Thus, we have two possibilities: Case (i): E is at the extreme left E ___ D __ G A F __ Case (ii): E is at extreme right __ __ D G A F ___ E","entity_count":8,"variables":1,"constraints":3,"case_splits":2,"resolution_type":"multiple","resolution_count":2,"information_load":"medium","solving_methodologies":["case_elimination","linear_sequencing"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E1B_Q004","question_text":"If there are three persons between B and H, then who is sitting to the left of D?","options":{"A":"B","B":"H","C":"C","D":"Cannot be determined"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"C","solution_text":"Three persons sitting between B and H is possible only in case (i) and then C will be sitting to the left of D.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q005","question_text":"If C is at one of the ends and B is adjacent to D, then how many persons are sitting between C and H?","options":{"A":"Three","B":"Zero","C":"Five","D":"Cannot be determined"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Cannot be determined","solution_text":"In case (i), if C is at the extreme end then B is adjacent to D. Then there can be either 3 or 5 persons sitting between C and H. Hence, cannot be determined.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q006","question_text":"If C is adjacent to G and H is at one of the ends, then who is third to the left of G?","options":{"A":"B","B":"D","C":"C","D":"Cannot be determined"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"B","solution_text":"C can be adjacent to G in case (i) only. And H is at the extreme end. Thus, B is third to the left of G.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":90}]},{"set_id":"LR_E1B_S7_11","exercise":"exercise_1b","type":"linear_arrangement","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. Exactly six persons from amongst five boys − A, B, C, D, E − and four girls − P, Q, R, S − are to sit in six chairs, which are arranged in a row from left to right, and the others stand. The following conditions are to be adhered to while making the arrangement. (i) No two girls sit in adjacent seats. (ii) Exactly three boys should be among those who are seated in these six chairs. (iii) A and P are seated next to each other. (iv) If E sits, then R also sits and vice-versa, but they do not sit next to each other. (v) If P or R sits, then Q will stand.","setup_solution":"Five boys – A, B, C, D, E and four girls – P, Q, R, S are to sit in 6 chairs arranged from left to right in a row and the remaining must stand. From condition (ii), we get that exactly 3 boys should sit, which means that exactly 3 girls also should be sitting. From condition (i), we also know that no two girls should in adjacent seats. From (iii), we know that A and P are seated next to each other. From (v), we get that if P or R sits, then Q stands. We need to find the three girls who sit out of P, Q, R and S. From (v), we know that Q has to stand always as either one of P or R will definitely be sitting. P, R, S are the girls who are sitting. From (iv), we get that if R sits then E sits, which means E is one of the boys sitting. The persons who are definitely sitting are A, P, R, S and E.","entity_count":6,"variables":2,"constraints":5,"case_splits":1,"resolution_type":"multiple","resolution_count":10,"information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["multi_constraint_balancing","trial_and_error_verification"],"type_specific":{"partial_resolution":true,"note":"Base deduction fixes WHO sits (A, P, R, S, E definite; one of B/C/D fills last seat) but not their seating order — order resolved per-question with additional constraints."},"questions":[{"id":"LR_E1B_Q007","question_text":"If C sits at the left end and A is sitting in the second seat from the right end, then who sits to the immediate right of A?","options":{"A":"P","B":"R","C":"Q","D":"Cannot be determined"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"R","solution_text":"It is given that C is at the extreme left end and A is second from the right. We get the following arrangement: 1 2 3 4 5 6 C A Since the girls don't sit adjacent to each other therefore 3 is occupied by a boy who happens to be E. We know, from (iv), that R does not sit next to E, which means R sits at 6. P is next to A (from (iii)), which means P is at 4 and the remaining place 2 is occupied by S. The final arrangement is as given below: 1 2 3 4 5 6 C S E P A R R is to the immediate right of A.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q008","question_text":"Which of the following is not a valid arrangement of persons sitting from left to right?","options":{"A":"P, A, E, S, C, R","B":"A, P, E, S, C, R","C":"S, E, P, A, R, D","D":"B, R, E, A, P, Q"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"B, R, E, A, P, Q","solution_text":"The best way to work out this question is through the choices and by applying the conditions to them. We find that choice (D) violates conditions (iv) and (v) hence it is not a valid arrangement whereas, all others conform to all the rules.","question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q009","question_text":"If D is second from the right end, then the total number of possible arrangements is","options":{"A":"Nine","B":"Seven","C":"Ten","D":"Five"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Ten","solution_text":"If D is sitting 2nd from the extreme right, then the possible arrangements are: (1) A P E S D R (2) E P A R D S (3) E P A S D R (4) E S A P D R (5) S E P A D R (6) R A P E D S (7) P A S E D R (8) S A P E D R (9) P A E S D R (10) S E A P D R They can sit in 10 different ways.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":150},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q010","question_text":"If P is sitting at the left end, then who could be sitting at the right end?","options":{"A":"R or E","B":"E or S","C":"S or R","D":"R or E or S"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"R or E or S","solution_text":"If P is sitting at the extreme left end, then we can have the following arrangements: P A R D/B/C S E P A S E B/C/D R P A R B/C/D E S Hence, either E or R or S sits at the extreme right end.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q011","question_text":"If it is known that S sits in the third seat from the left end and B sits in the second seat from the right, end then who sits exactly next to two girls?","options":{"A":"A","B":"E","C":"B","D":"Data inadequate"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"A","solution_text":"With the given data we get the following arrangement: 1 2 3 4 5 6 S B Since the girls don't sit adjacent to each other, it means that places 1 and 6 are occupied by the girls P and R. It is given that A and P always sit together, which means P cannot be at 6. P is at 1, A is at 2 and R is at 6 which leaves us with E at 4. The final arrangement is as follows: 1 2 3 4 5 6 P A S E B R A is the person sitting next to two girls.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120}]},{"set_id":"LR_E1B_S12_14","exercise":"exercise_1b","type":"linear_arrangement","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. A certain number of persons are sitting in a straight line and are facing north. The following information is known about them. Four persons sit between P and B, who sits three places away from K. B sits exactly between R and K. R sits to the right of P, who sits two places away from O. The number of persons who sit to the left of O is the same as the number of persons who sit between R and P. K sits five places away to the left of E, who sits to the immediate left of U. The number of persons who sit to the left of P is the same as the number of persons who sit to the right of U.","setup_solution":"It is given that four persons sit between P and B, who sits three places away from K. B sits exactly between R and K. K sits five places away from E, who sits to the immediate left of U. R sits to the right of P, who sits two places away from O, From the above information, we can say that P sits fifth to the left of B. R and K sit third to the left and third to the right of B in any order. O sits second to the left of P. Also given that the number of persons who sit to the left of O is the same as the number of persons who sit between R and P. In case (1), since seven persons sit between R and P, hence seven persons sit to the left of O. In case (2), since one person sits between R and P, hence only one person sits to the left of O. From this, we can say that E sits fifth to the right of K in both the cases. From this, we get the following possible arrangements, Case 1: Case 2: Also given that K sits five places away to the left of E, who sits to the immediate left of U. From this we can say that in case (1), E sits fifth to the right of K and since there is no place for U, hence it is eliminated. In case (2), E sits either fifth to the left of K or fifth to the right of K. Also given that the number of persons who sit to the left of P is the same as the number of persons who sit to the right of U. From this, we can say that E sits fifth to the right of K and U sits to the immediate right of E and since there are three persons sit to the left of P, hence three persons sit to the right of U. Therefore, there are 22 persons sitting in the row.","entity_count":22,"variables":1,"constraints":8,"case_splits":2,"resolution_type":"single","information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["case_elimination","linear_sequencing"],"type_specific":{"unstated_entity_count":true,"note":"Total number of people in the row is not given directly and must itself be derived through the constraint chain before final positions can be pinned down. This derivation-of-N step is itself a dependency layer, contributing to overall complexity beyond what entity_count alone reflects."},"questions":[{"id":"LR_E1B_Q012","question_text":"How many persons sit to the left of B?","options":{"A":"Ten","B":"Nine","C":"Eight","D":"Seven"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Eight","solution_text":"Eight persons sit to the left of B.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q013","question_text":"How many persons are sitting in the row?","options":{"A":"21","B":"18","C":"25","D":"20"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"21","solution_text":"21 persons are sitting in the row.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q014","question_text":"If B and E interchange their positions, then what is the position of P with respect to E?","options":{"A":"Third to the right","B":"Fourth to the left","C":"Immediate left","D":"Fifth to the left"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Fifth to the left","solution_text":"If B and E interchange their positions, then P sits fifth to the left of E.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120}]},{"set_id":"LR_E1B_S15_18","exercise":"exercise_1b","type":"linear_arrangement","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. Eight persons of a family – A through H – sit in a row facing north but not necessarily in the same order. The following information is known about them. Only two persons sit between B and her husband. Either B or B's husband sits at the end. H sits to the right of B, but not to the right of B's husband. B's husband sits to the immediate right of his father-in-law, A, who is married to G. F has only two sons but has no siblings. E, who is the brother-in-law of F sits two places away from B. The number of persons sitting to the right of B is the same as the number of persons sitting to the left of D, who is the paternal aunt of E. C is the son of B and does not sit adjacent to E.","setup_solution":"It is given that only two persons sit between B and her husband. Either B or B's husband sits at the end. H sits to the right of B, but not to the right of B's husband. B's husband sits to the immediate right of his father-in-law A, who is married to G. From the above information, we get two possible cases. In case (1), B sits at the left end, H sits second from the left end, A sits third from the left end and B's husband sits fourth from the left end. In case (2), B's husband sits at the right end, A sits second from the right end, H sits third from the right end and B sits fourth from the right end. Also given that F has only two sons but has no siblings. E, who is the brother-in-law of F sits two places away from B. From this, we can say that case (1) is eliminated since we cannot place E. Hence in case (2), E sits third from the left end. Also given that the number of persons sit to the right of B is the same as the number of persons sit to the left of D, who is the paternal aunt of E. From this, we can say that D sits to the immediate left of B. Since C is the son of B and does not sit adjacent to E, C sits at the left end, F is B's husband, G sits second from the left end and H is the other son of B.","entity_count":8,"variables":2,"constraints":8,"case_splits":2,"resolution_type":"single","information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["case_elimination","relational_decoding"],"type_specific":{"requires_relationship_decoding":true,"note":"Clues are given as family relationships (father-in-law, brother-in-law, paternal aunt) that must first be decoded into identity/role facts before they function as positional constraints. Failure can occur at the relationship-decoding step independent of the seating-arrangement step."},"questions":[{"id":"LR_E1B_Q015","question_text":"How is C related to A?","options":{"A":"Nephew","B":"Niece","C":"Grandson","D":"Granddaughter"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Grandson","solution_text":"C is the grandson of A.","question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q016","question_text":"What is the position of G with respect to her husband?","options":{"A":"Third to the right","B":"Fourth to the right","C":"Second to the right","D":"Fifth to the left"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Fifth to the left","solution_text":"G's husband is A and G sits fifth to the left of A.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q017","question_text":"Three of the following are alike in a certain way and hence form a group. Find the one that does not belong to that group.","options":{"A":"H","B":"E","C":"G","D":"C"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"G","solution_text":"Except G, the remaining persons are males.","question_operation":"odd_one_out","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q018","question_text":"Which of the following is definitely true?","options":{"A":"E sits second to the right of his brother-in-law.","B":"A sits to the immediate right of his grandson.","C":"H is the granddaughter of G.","D":"Only two persons sit between E and D."},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"A sits to the immediate right of his grandson.","solution_text":"That 'A sits to the immediate right of his grandson' is definitely true.","question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90}]},{"set_id":"LR_E1B_S19_22","exercise":"exercise_1b","type":"linear_arrangement","is_set":true,"setup_text":"Eight friends Amiya, Bharat, Chandu, Dheeraj, Ezhil, Farhan, Gaurav, and Harish are standing in a row facing towards the North. The following information is known about them. (1) None among Chandu, Ezhil and Amiya stands at the ends. (2) If the positions of Chandu and Farhan are interchanged each of them gets exactly one new neighbour. (3) Amiya's position is one removed from Bharat's position. Amiya is not to the right of Bharat. (4) Only one person is standing to the right of Dheeraj. (5) Exactly one person stands between Farhan and Harish. (6) At least one person stands between Chandu and Farhan.","setup_solution":"From 2, 4 and 6, we get the following three cases, Case 1: Case 2: Case 3: From 3, Amiya and Bharat sit adjacent to each other from the left end respectively. From 1, case 2 gets eliminated since Amiya does not sit at the end. Case 1: Case 3: From 5, case 1 gets eliminated. Case 3: From 1, Ezhil sits between Chandu and Farhan and Gaurav sits at the left end.","entity_count":8,"variables":1,"constraints":6,"case_splits":3,"resolution_type":"single","information_load":"medium","solving_methodologies":["case_elimination","linear_sequencing"],"questions":[{"id":"LR_E1B_Q019","question_text":"How many persons sit between Chandu and Dheeraj?","options":null,"correct_answer":"2","correct_answer_value":"2","solution_text":"Two persons sit between Chandu and Dheeraj.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"TITA","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":60},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q020","question_text":"What is the position of Bharat with respect to Ezhil?","options":{"A":"Second to the left","B":"Second to the right","C":"Immediate right","D":"Fourth to the left"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Second to the left","solution_text":"Bharat sits second to the left of Ezhil.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":60},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q021","question_text":"If the positions of Gaurav and Farhan are interchanged, then who among the following sits to the right of Gaurav?","options":{"A":"Amiya","B":"None","C":"Harish","D":"Ezhil"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Harish","solution_text":"If the positions of Gaurav and Farhan are interchanged, then Harish sits second to the right of Gaurav.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":75},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q022","question_text":"Which of the following statement(s) is/are true? Statement I: Amiya sits second to the left of Dheeraj. Statement II: Exactly two persons are sitting between Gaurav and Bharat.","options":{"A":"Only I","B":"Only II","C":"Both I and II","D":"Neither I nor II"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Neither I nor II","solution_text":"None of the statements is true.","question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":75}]},{"set_id":"LR_E1B_S23_26","exercise":"exercise_1b","type":"linear_arrangement","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. Four boys K, L, M, and N sit in row – I facing North and they are of different professions among engineer, doctor, professor and actor. Four girls P, Q, R, and S sit in row – II facing south and they are of different professions among lawyer, teacher, director, and collector. They sit in such a way that the distance between any two adjacent persons in a row is the same such that one person in one row faces the other a person in the other row, but not necessarily in the same order. Collector sits opposite the person who sits third to the right of N. Doctor and teacher sit opposite each other. Engineer sits opposite the person who sits third to the left of R. Only one person sits between K and L. R sits second to the right of S, the director. P does not sit opposite engineer and K is neither an engineer nor a doctor. Lawyer does not sit opposite actor.","setup_solution":"It is given that Collector sits opposite the person who sits third to the right of N, and Engineer sits opposite the person who sits third to the left of R and only one person sits between K and L. R __ __ __ __ Collector N K/L M L/K Engineer R sits second to the right of S and P does not sit opposite the Engineer and S is the director. R P S Q N K/L M L/K Doctor sits opposite to the Teacher and K is neither an Engineer nor a Doctor. Hence the final arrangement is as follows. Teacher Lawyer Director Collector R P S Q K M L Doctor professor Actor Engineer","entity_count":8,"variables":3,"constraints":8,"case_splits":1,"resolution_type":"single","information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["multi_constraint_balancing","linear_sequencing"],"type_specific":{"attribute_layers":2,"note":"Double-row structure with two attributes tracked beyond position: profession (distinct sets per row) and the opposite-row pairing. Variables counted as the independent free dimensions: Row I order, Row II order, profession-to-Row-I assignment (3, since K's profession is excluded early) -- treated here as 3 combined dimensions per the attribute_layers framing rather than raw entity count."},"questions":[{"id":"LR_E1B_Q023","question_text":"Who is the doctor?","options":{"A":"K","B":"M","C":"L","D":"N"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"N","solution_text":"N is the Doctor.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q024","question_text":"Who sits opposite the director?","options":{"A":"Actor","B":"Professor","C":"L","D":"K"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Actor","solution_text":"Actor sits opposite Director.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q025","question_text":"Which of the following 'person–profession' combination is correct?","options":{"A":"P – Director","B":"S – Collector","C":"M – Actor","D":"N – Engineer"},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"M – Actor","solution_text":"'M – Actor' combination is true.","question_operation":"statement_verification","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q026","question_text":"What is the position of P with respect to R?","options":{"A":"Immediate right","B":"Immediate left","C":"Second to the right","D":"Second to the left"},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Immediate left","solution_text":"P sits to the immediate left of R.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90}]},{"set_id":"LR_E1B_S27_30","exercise":"exercise_1b","type":"linear_arrangement","is_set":true,"setup_text":"These questions are based on the following information. Six people A, B, C, D, E and F, each of a different weight among 60, 80, 75, 58, 82 and 96 kgs(not necessarily in the given order), sit in a row facing north. The following details are known about them: I. The sum of weights of no two adjacent persons is more than 156 kgs. II. A, the person with the least weight is third to the left of C. III. Neither A nor C is an immediate neighbour of B. IV. D and E are not neighbours. Directions for questions 27 and 28: Write your answer in the input box provided below the question. Directions for questions 29 and 30: Select the correct alternative from the given choices.","setup_solution":"Let us number the positions 1 to 6 from left to right. From II, A and C can be in position (1, 4), (2, 5), or (3, 6). Positions (2, 5) are not possible, because from III, B should not be adjacent to either A or C. If positions (1, 4) are considered, then A (58 kg) will be in position 1. From I, the person whose weight is 96 kg can be adjacent to the persons whose weights are 58 kg or 60 kg only. Hence, the persons whose weights are 96 and 60 will be in positions 2 and 3, respectively. But in this case, the persons whose weights are 75 kg, 80 kg and 82 kg will be in positions 4, 5, and 6 in any order. But the person whose weight is 82 kg cannot be adjacent to the person whose weight is 75 kg or 80 kg. Hence, A and C cannot be in positions (1, 4). Thus, A and C should be in positions (3, 6) in that order. Thus, we get the following. 1 2 3 4 5 6 A (58) C From III, B should be in position 1. Let us check where the person whose weight is 96 kg can be placed. If the person whose weight is 96 kg is in position 1 or 2, then the person whose weight is 60 kg should be in position 2 or 1. But in this case the persons whose weights are 75 kg, 80 kg and 82 kg will be in positions 4, 5, and 6. This violates condition I. Hence, the person whose weight is 96 kg cannot be in position 1 or 2. If the person whose weight is 96 kg is in position 4, then the persons whose weights are 60 kg and 82 kg should be in positions 5 and 6, respectively. If the person whose weight is 96 kg is in position 5, then the persons whose weight is 82 kg will be in position 4 or 6. But here condition I will be violated. Hence, the person whose weight is 96 kg cannot be inposition 5. If the person whose weight is 96 kg is in position 6, then the persons whose weights are 60 kg and 82 kg should be in positions 5 and 4, respectively. Thus, we get the following. 1 2 3 4 5 6 75/80 80/75 A (58) 96/82 60 C (82/96) Since D and E are not adjacent to each other (condition IV), one among D and E should be in position 2. Thus, the final arrangement is as below. 1 2 3 4 5 6 B (75/80) D/E (80/75) A (58) D/E/F (96/82) D/E/F (60) C (82/96)","entity_count":6,"variables":2,"constraints":4,"case_splits":3,"resolution_type":"multiple","resolution_count":4,"information_load":"high","solving_methodologies":["case_elimination","multi_constraint_balancing"],"type_specific":{"note":"Two attributes tracked simultaneously: position and weight assignment, with weight-sum constraint (condition I) requiring continuous cross-checking against adjacent pairs rather than a single direct clue."},"questions":[{"id":"LR_E1B_Q027","question_text":"In how many ways can the six people be seated?","options":null,"correct_answer":"4","correct_answer_value":"4","solution_text":"3! = 6 ways are possible. But as D and E cannot be together, 2 possibilities are eliminated. Therefore, 4 ways are possible.","question_operation":"count_arrangements","answer_type":"TITA","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q028","question_text":"If D and E are the immediate neighbours of A, what is the weight of F (in Kgs)?","options":null,"correct_answer":"60","correct_answer_value":"60","solution_text":"Weight of F would be 60 kgs.","question_operation":"hypothetical","answer_type":"TITA","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":120},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q029","question_text":"Who is second to the left of A?","options":{"A":"B","B":"C","C":"D","D":"E"},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"B","solution_text":"B is second to the left of A.","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"medium","time_benchmark_seconds":75},{"id":"LR_E1B_Q030","question_text":"What is the sum of the weights of the people at the ends?","options":{"A":"155","B":"162","C":"142","D":"Cannot be determined"},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Cannot be determined","solution_text":"The sum of the weights of the people at the ends is 75 + 96 = 171 or 80 + 96 = 176","question_operation":"position_lookup","answer_type":"mcq","difficulty":"hard","time_benchmark_seconds":90}]}]`);export{e as default};
